# Radagast of Rhosgobel: "The first creature spell you cast each turn costs {2} less to cast and can be cast as though it had
# flash" - only its controller's spells, and only theirs counted. On turn 2 Bot2's Grizzly Bears, Bot2's first creature spell
# that turn, costs its full {1}{G} (two Moxen pay it exactly, none left floating). It is not one Bot1 cast, so at the end of that
# turn Bot1's own Grizzly Bears is still the first and is flashed in for {G}. On turn 3 Bot2 is refused a creature spell in Bot1's
# main phase, with a Mox Emerald and a Mox Jet untapped to pay for it: Radagast gives Bot2 no flash.

